Kobalt, an alternative reader for Kobo firmware 4, 5 and 6.

The default build opens DRM-free EPUBs, including DRM-free Kobo purchases.
Nickel checks access; Kobalt reads the unencrypted EPUB resources directly.
Protected books show a short handoff screen, then open in Nickel's reader.
Previews, PDFs and unsupported formats open directly in Nickel's reader.
A loading failure offers Try built-in reader or Go back.

Reading Settings has a Kobalt section at the top. Open books in Kobalt
is on after installation. Turn it off to use Nickel's reader for later
books. The choice is saved in config.json in this folder. Long-press a
book to open it once with the other reader.

Tap the left or right third of the page to turn pages, or swipe. Tap the
middle or the title for the menus. The bottom tabs open Chapters, Text,
Layout, Light, Stats and Search. Settings is at the top.

Fonts and their manifest are in assets/. Settings and saved positions are
the other .json files in this folder. Kobalt also saves your position to
Nickel when you leave a book.

To remove Kobalt, delete the file uninstall, or this whole folder, and
restart the device. Saved positions and settings stay unless you delete
the folder. A temporary test build creates uninstall-now and removes
itself on the next restart. To install a new build over a temporary one,
delete uninstall-now before you eject.

If Kobalt stops during startup or while a book is open, it leaves
startup-session or active-session.json here. While either file exists,
Kobalt stays off and Nickel's reader is used. Look at the logs first,
then delete the file and restart to try Kobalt again.

events.jsonl and events.jsonl.previous record what Kobalt did, at most
128 KiB each. They contain no book text or account data. state.json and
session.json can contain book identifiers; keep them private.
